    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>\(d_x=l_x-l_{x+1}\)</p>
<p>To find the value \(d_{x1}\), we get the difference of \(l_{x2}\) and \(l_{x1}\), example \(d_{x1}={@l_x1@}-{@l_x2@}={@d_x1@}\) </p>
<p>To find the values of \(q_x\) we use the formula \(q_x=\displaystyle \frac{d_x}{l_x}\)</p>
<p>To find the value of \(p_x\) we use the formula \(p_x=1-q_x\) or \(p_x=\displaystyle \frac{l_{x+1}}{l_x}\)</p>
<p>Example \(p_{x1}=1-{@decimalplaces(q_x1,4)@}={@decimalplaces(p_x1,4)@}\)</p>
<p>We use the formula \(l_x​=l_{x−1​}−d_{x−1}\) to find the values of \(l_x\)​</p>
<br>
<p>Using the formulas above, you can find all the values required in the table.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
